-- Appendix T directory suite (packageMode).
-- Robustness/degenerate input: a TRULY EMPTY source file (lib.kp is
-- zero bytes — no header, no declarations, not even a newline) is a
-- valid module.  §8.1: with no module header the module name is the
-- path-derived name (`lib`), so `import lib` resolves; a module with
-- zero declarations is not an error, and the importing module still
-- elaborates and answers type queries.  (The header-only empty module
-- is covered by KITTEN-empty-program-accepted; the zero-byte file in a
-- package was previously untested.)
--! mode check
--! packageMode
--! assertNoErrors
--! assertType main.x Int
